Track 1: Molten Glass Swallows the Rail
- Story & Context: On a rain-slicked Tuesday journey aboard the midnight express out of Santos, Ysabel patched her pocket synth directly into a brass trumpet's pick-up mic, capturing the instant an overheating train brake emitted a high-pitched metallic scream that tuned perfectly to a C-major 9th chord. The track captures that exact moment of panic turning into bliss, as tired commuters began tapping their rings on the aluminum handrails to form a syncopated bossa beat. By the time the train rolled into Central, thirty strangers were humming the same weightless lullaby in perfect harmony. Ysabel recorded the conductor crying softly into his intercom, repeating the now-famous line, "A noite não tem fim, só tem metal e luz" ("The night has no end, it only has metal and light").
