Track 2: Stained Starlight Through the Broken Transom
- Story & Context: Written during a fourteen-hour delay in an abandoned railway depot in Niterói, Caio locked himself in an unused glassblower's shed to record the sound of cool sea air rushing through cracked, stained-glass windows. He sampled his own erratic heartbeat using a 2010s sampler app, overlaying it with breathy flugelhorn swells that mimic the slow cresting of bay waves against rusted train cars. The song tells the story of Mateo, a legendary train conductor who allegedly lost his hearing but could still feel the sub-bass frequencies of the pocket synths through the floorboards. The vocal track features Caio's partner whispering over a drifting nylon guitar, softly chanting, "Did you see the stained light crack before we hit the station?"
