Track 3: The Silica-Breath of Station 09
- Story & Context: The final track serves as an urban myth set in a non-existent station that commuters claim only appears on the map when the pocket synths run down to their last one percent of battery life. Recorded entirely using dead-battery voltage drops that caused the pitch of the synths to sag and bend like warm vinyl, the brass section sounds like ancient organ pipes dissolving into ocean mist. The band recorded the finale in a single, unedited take as their train coasted with its engines killed through a fog-choked valley. A quiet chorus of ghostly, pitch-shifted voices closes the EP with the lingering question, "Where do the sleepers go when the last car uncouples?"
